Expected after fix: content-desc="1 stars" .. "5 stars" on each clickable star; button role.
Observed: empty desc, and role degraded to class=View (button:true NOT propagated either).
The MergeSemantics(Semantics(label:'N stars', button:true, child: InkWell(child: bare Icon)))
wrapping produced ZERO change vs cycle 0.

Contrast (same store screen, same build): AC5 toggle uses PLAIN
Semantics(button:true, selected:sel, label:'Grid view'/'List view', child: InkWell(child: Container(Icon)))
and DOES project -> class=Button, content-desc present, selected state exposed. WORKS.

Root-cause lead for the engineer: the two failing sites (AC3 zoom, AC4 stars) share the pattern
MergeSemantics > Semantics(label,button) > InkWell > BARE Icon. The passing sites (AC5 toggle,
AC9 badge, home icons) use plain Semantics with a non-bare child (Container(Icon) / Image).
On-device, the bare-Icon MergeSemantics wrap drops the label AND the button role. Recommend
switching the failing sites to the proven AC5 pattern (plain Semantics wrapping InkWell whose
child is wrapped, or Semantics(container:true,...)) rather than MergeSemantics, and re-verifying
live with uiautomator dump — NOT the widget test, which passes regardless (test +5 green).
